{"step_index":67,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-07T07:42:58Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-07T14:42:58+07:00\nCompleted At: 2026-10-07T14:42:58+07:00\nFile Path: `file:///e:/codekids/node_modules/next/dist/docs/01-app/03-api-reference/03-file-conventions/02-route-segment-config/instant.md`\nTotal Lines: 178\nTotal Bytes: 9502\nShowing lines 1 to 178\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: ---\n2: title: instant\n3: description: Configure instant navigation validation for a route segment.\n4: related:\n5:   title: Next Steps\n6:   description: Learn how to use instant navigations in practice.\n7:   links:\n8:     - app/guides/instant-navigation\n9:     - app/api-reference/file-conventions/route-segment-config/ensureStatic\n10:     - app/getting-started/caching\n11:     - app/getting-started/revalidating\n12:     - app/api-reference/directives/use-cache\n13: ---\n14: \n15: The `instant` route segment config controls how Next.js validates whether a navigation into this segment would produce an instant UI.\n16: \n17: Next.js uses prefetching to preload navigations for all in-app links on the current page. However, client-side data fetching or partially prerendered results from the server can lead to navigations that don't update the UI immediately. To help you build fast-feeling navigations, `instant` lets you tell Next.js what to expect from navigations through the configured segment. For instance, you can indicate that navigations into this segment should produce a UI that renders instantly without waiting on any externally loaded data. You can also indicate that navigations aren't expected to be instant.\n18: \n19: When a segment is configured to expect an instant UI, Next.js surfaces any code in your application that would block the navigation from updating the UI immediately. See the [Instant Navigation guide](/docs/app/guides/instant-navigation) for an end-to-end walkthrough.\n20: \n21: > **Good to know*\n<truncated 6789 bytes>\n both page refreshes and link clicks to check that your loading states look right on first visit and on navigation.\n143: \n144: ## Testing instant navigation\n145: \n146: The `@next/playwright` package exports an `instant()` helper that holds back dynamic content while the callback runs against the instant UI. The testing API is available automatically in development. For a production build, enable [`experimental.exposeTestingApiInProductionBuild`](/docs/app/api-reference/config/next-config-js/exposeTestingApiInProductionBuild) in the test build. See the [guide](/docs/app/guides/instant-navigation#prevent-regressions-with-e2e-tests) for a full example.\n147: \n148: ```typescript\n149: import { instant } from '@next/playwright'\n150: ```\n151: \n152: {/* TODO: remove when fixed and from prod-docs-release */}\n153: \n154: ## Known issue: shared cookie across projects\n155: \n156: The DevTools use a `next-instant-navigation-testing` cookie to hold back dynamic content and freeze the page at the instant UI. Because cookies are scoped to the domain and not the port, running multiple projects on the same domain (typically `localhost`) means the cookie is shared across them and can cause unexpected behavior. Clear the cookie or close the Navigation Inspector panel when switching between projects to avoid issues.\n157: \n158: > **Good to know:** This will be fixed as part of stabilizing the feature.\n159: \n160: ## TypeScript\n161: \n162: ```tsx\n163: type InstantConfig =\n164:   | true\n165:   | false\n166:   | {\n167:       level?: 'warning'\n168:     }\n169: \n170: export const instant: InstantConfig = true\n171: ```\n172: \n173: ## Version History\n174: \n175: | Version   | Changes                                                                            |\n176: | --------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n177: | `v16.3.0` | `instant` export stabilized, replacing `unstable_instant` (Cache Components only). |\n178: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
